# Line endings are part of the contract, not a local preference.
#
# The check scripts slice declarations out of `index.js` and `client.js` with
# markers written as `\n...`, and several of them (and every `mutate-*` script)
# match multi-line source text literally. Those patterns are authored in LF.
# On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` the working tree is CRLF, so
# a pattern that spans a line break silently stops matching: the check reports
# "no closing bracket in column 0", or the mutation runner reports
# PATTERN-MISSING and scores a guard as unproven. That is exactly how the first
# CI run went red on `windows-latest` while `ubuntu-latest` stayed green.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree on every platform, so what CI checks
# out is what the patterns were written against.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be line-ending converted at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary
